{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JU28vFzt2y4EjjDn8612of","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Node.js latest LTS version release\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Software 43949 Published by\",\"url\":\"https://www.linuxcompatible.org/story/nodejs-v20196-lts-released\"},{\"title\":\"Node.js v20.19.5 (LTS) released\",\"url\":\"https://www.warp2search.net/story/nodejs-v20195-lts-released\"},{\"title\":\"endoflife.date\",\"url\":\"https://endoflife.date/nodejs%20\"},{\"title\":\"Software 43969 Published by\",\"url\":\"https://www.linuxcompatible.org/story/nodejs-2520-current-and-24111-lts-released\"},{\"title\":\"endoflife.date\",\"url\":\"https://endoflife.date/nodejs\"},{\"title\":\"releasealert.dev\",\"url\":\"https://releasealert.dev/chocolatey/Node.js%20LTS%20%28Install%29\"},{\"title\":\"Node.js-Releases, Versionen und End-of-Life-Termine (EOL)\",\"url\":\"https://www.versio.io/de/product-release-end-of-life-eol-openjs-foundation-nodejs.html\"}]\n\nThe search results point to Node.js 26 as the newest LTS line, but the sources disagree on the exact version number.\n\n- **Node.js 26:** One source says 26 2026-05-05 13 26.8.2 2026-09-09 Ja, which lists 26.8.2 as the latest version with LTS status. A separate endoflife.date snapshot lists 26.12.1 (21 Oct 2026) but labels 26 as \"Upcoming LTS,\" which conflicts with the other source's LTS status. The snapshot may be older, so check nodejs.org for the definitive answer.\n- **Release cadence:** After six months, releases after 26 move to Active LTS status and are ready for general use.\n- **Older LTS lines:** Node 24 and 22 are still listed as LTS. The Chocolatey LTS package lists 24.16.0 and 22.22.3 as stable builds. Node 20 and 24.11.1 appear in older articles, so they are likely outdated.\n- **Production guidance:** Production applications should only use Active LTS or Maintenance LTS releases.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b23b534d-bac2-413d-8532-e419513c5350","uuid":"3238a718-3dbd-4273-aa51-316ef023ee20","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:01:31.953Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Node.js latest LTS version release","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014Jf6Vq3ZqvX2WkQ31BS79c","content":[{"title":"Software 43949 Published by","url":"https://www.linuxcompatible.org/story/nodejs-v20196-lts-released"},{"title":"Node.js v20.19.5 (LTS) released","url":"https://www.warp2search.net/story/nodejs-v20195-lts-released"},{"title":"endoflife.date","url":"https://endoflife.date/nodejs%20"},{"title":"Software 43969 Published by","url":"https://www.linuxcompatible.org/story/nodejs-2520-current-and-24111-lts-released"},{"title":"endoflife.date","url":"https://endoflife.date/nodejs"},{"title":"releasealert.dev","url":"https://releasealert.dev/chocolatey/Node.js%20LTS%20%28Install%29"},{"title":"Node.js-Releases, Versionen und End-of-Life-Termine (EOL)","url":"https://www.versio.io/de/product-release-end-of-life-eol-openjs-foundation-nodejs.html"}]},"The search results point to Node.js 26 as the newest LTS line, but the sources disagree on the exact version number.\n\n- **Node.js 26:** One source says 26 2026-05-05 13 26.8.2 2026-09-09 Ja, which lists 26.8.2 as the latest version with LTS status. A separate endoflife.date snapshot lists 26.12.1 (21 Oct 2026) but labels 26 as \"Upcoming LTS,\" which conflicts with the other source's LTS status. The snapshot may be older, so check nodejs.org for the definitive answer.\n- **Release cadence:** After six months, releases after 26 move to Active LTS status and are ready for general use.\n- **Older LTS lines:** Node 24 and 22 are still listed as LTS. The Chocolatey LTS package lists 24.16.0 and 22.22.3 as stable builds. Node 20 and 24.11.1 appear in older articles, so they are likely outdated.\n- **Production guidance:** Production applications should only use Active LTS or Maintenanc